# Always push to GitHub

The client (repository collaborator) reviews and edits this project directly on GitHub (`ersanjt/pipolune`). Local-only work is invisible to her.

- After every completed change, run `npm run build` if site code changed, then commit and push to `origin main`.
- Before starting work, `git pull --rebase origin main` — the client may have pushed changes.
- Commit messages: short imperative English, e.g. `Add catalogue filter panel`, `Update approved style v1.2`.
- Pushing to `main` deploys to https://pipolune.com automatically (`.github/workflows/ci.yml` → `scripts/deploy.mjs`, SFTP). Check the run with `gh run watch`.
- Never commit `private/`, `.env*` (except `*.example`), SSH keys, passwords, cPanel credentials, invoices or personal data. Server credentials live only in GitHub Actions secrets.
- File naming: lowercase kebab-case; language suffix before extension (`*.ru.md`, `*.en.md`); versions as `v1.1`.
- Design source of truth: `docs/brand/approved-style-v1.1.ru.md` and `docs/uiux/uiux-foundation-v1.ru.md`. The older `docs/product/website-brief-v0.en.md` visual sections are superseded.
